  "worked_solution": "The given polar curve is the polar rose with $5$ petals, and we know that the area of the first petal is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /10}^{\\pi /10}{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226336/assets/428af134250df6268b97998db880e33f88a6b5bd32859036e29e04fc1861e0c9.png)\n\nTherefore, the total area bounded by the polar curve is\n\n$$\n{A}_{\\text{total}}=5\\cdot A=\\frac{45}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /10}^{\\pi /10}{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$",
